# CODEOWNERS — sensitive-path gate (FOX-3319 / supply-chain audit P1 R5).
#
# Order matters: later patterns override earlier ones. The catch-all at the
# bottom intentionally requires maintainer review on EVERY PR; per-path
# entries above it tighten that to specific reviewer sets.
#
# Replace @mindstone-engineering/<team> placeholders with the real GitHub
# team slugs once those teams exist on the org. Keep at least one human
# fallback owner per critical path so PRs are never auto-mergeable.

# --- CI / release pipeline. Compromise = arbitrary publish. -----------------
/.github/                                @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
/.github/workflows/                      @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS                      @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers

# --- Dependency surface per connector. Lockfile drives what the publish ----
#     job installs; package.json drives lifecycle hooks. Both gate on
#     maintainer review.
/connectors/*/package.json               @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
/connectors/*/package-lock.json          @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
/connectors/_template/                   @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers

# --- Legal & security posture. ---------------------------------------------
/LICENSE                                 @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
/SECURITY.md                             @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
/docs/security/                          @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers

# --- Shared test harness ships into every connector's devDependencies. -----
/test-harness/                           @mindstone-engineering/oss-maintainers
